<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.African November retail sales rise 3.9 pct m/m.</title>
<headline>S.African November retail sales rise 3.9 pct m/m.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>South African retail trade sales rose a seasonally adjusted 3.9 percent month-on-month in November to 11.88 billion rand, latest Central Statistical Service (CSS) data shows.</p>
<p>Year-on-year, seasonally adjusted retail sales were up 12.8 percent from 10.53 billion rand in November 1995, the CSS said.</p>
<p>On an actual basis, retail trade sales were up 8.5 percent month-on-month and up 13 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>Retail trade sales at current prices.</p>
<p>(rand million):</p>
<p>				 Nov '96	 Oct '96	Nov '95</p>
<p>    Seasonally adjusted  11,877.0	11,430.4     10,525.7</p>
<p>    Actual		   12,279.3	11,312.9     10,870.6</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom, +27 11 482-1003</p>
